		/// <summary>The GetHostNameW function retrieves the standard host name for the local computer as a Unicode string.</summary>
		/// <param name="name">A pointer to a buffer that receives the local host name as a <b>null</b>-terminated Unicode string.</param>
		/// <param name="namelen">The length, in wide characters, of the buffer pointed to by the <i>name</i> parameter.</param>
		/// <returns>
		/// <para>If no error occurs, <b>GetHostNameW</b> returns zero. Otherwise, it returns <b>SOCKET_ERROR</b> and a specific error code can be retrieved by calling <a href="https://docs.microsoft.com/windows/desktop/api/winsock/nf-winsock-wsagetlasterror">WSAGetLastError</a>. </para>
		/// <para>This doc was truncated.</para>
